NEARS-2298 QA — AC3 finding: cm-firebase-token snackbar is IDENTICAL pre-fix (302) and post-fix (401)
Repro: customer@nears.com (user_id 6) logs in on-device; the exact minted oauth_access_tokens
row is then revoked (revoked=1) on an ISOLATED DB copy (multi_food_db_qa2298, NOT the shared
dev DB); app is cold-booted (am force-stop + am start) with the stale token still in local
secure storage.

=== POST-FIX (401, HEAD 3dfac576) — emulator-5564, pid 23013 ===
08-21 23:39:01.455 [NET] endpoint=/api/v1/customer/cm-firebase-token http_status=401
08-21 23:39:01.652 [FAIL] endpoint=/api/v1/customer/cm-firebase-token http_status=401 type=ApiFailure msg="unhandled api response" correlation_id=f883295e-9fe6-484d-8b96-35d814fb74e3
08-21 23:39:01.678 #1      showCustomSnackBar (package:sixam_mart/common/widgets/custom_snackbar.dart:30:17)
08-21 23:39:01.685 [ERR] msg="error snackbar shown"

=== PRE-FIX (302, parent commit 47c7346e, Admin/bootstrap/app.php reverted for this run only,
    restored to HEAD immediately after) — same device, pid 23927, fresh stale-token repro ===
08-21 23:43:29.122 [NET] endpoint=/api/v1/customer/cm-firebase-token http_status=302
08-21 23:43:29.173 [FAIL] endpoint=/api/v1/customer/cm-firebase-token http_status=302 type=ApiFailure msg="unhandled api response" correlation_id=964e0c72-b056-48f9-bfc2-a8215ba6c57e
08-21 23:43:29.180 #1      showCustomSnackBar (package:sixam_mart/common/widgets/custom_snackbar.dart:30:17)
08-21 23:43:29.182 [ERR] msg="error snackbar shown"

Root cause (read, not just observed): UserApp/lib/features/auth/controllers/auth_controller.dart
lines 297-305 — `_forLoggedInUserRouteProcess()` (splash_route_helper.dart:81) fires
`Get.find<AuthController>().updateToken()` UNAWAITED on every logged-in cold boot. That method's
own success check is `response.statusCode == 200` (auth_service.dart:92-97) — true for neither a
302 redirect nor a 401 JSON, so BOTH produce `success=false` and both trigger the SAME
`showCustomSnackBar('sorry_something_went_wrong'.tr)` at auth_controller.dart:303. This path is
entirely independent of the NEARS-2298 exception-handler change (Admin/bootstrap/app.php) — the
snackbar fires identically whether the backend answers 302 or 401.

Conclusion: AC3 ("no error snackbar ... on the first screen") is NOT satisfied by the shipped
fix on the real stale-token repro. The defect is pre-existing (present at parent commit
47c7346e too, unrelated to this diff) — filed as a task_bug because it is the ticket's own
explicit AC3 deliverable and remains open, though the actual code that needs to change lives in
UserApp's AuthController/updateToken, outside this diff's Admin/bootstrap/app.php scope.
